 Joanna mentioned a page with dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness for her next movie; she finds the story deep and emotional.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n  - loss: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, causing her to feel bummed out. The existing summary mentioned sadness and loss.\n  - brother: Joanna's brother wrote something that brings back sweet memories, as he used to make her cute notes as a child.\n  - this: Nate won a large video game tournament last week, earning a lot of money from it. Joanna congratulated him.\n  - major company: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which bummed her out. Nate asked if something specific happened with the company.\n  - thoughts: Joanna uses writing as an escape to express feelings, put down thoughts, and heal, making something good from her thoughts and feelings.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - stories: Joanna finds happiness and fulfillment in creating stories and watching them come alive, calling writing a blessing for her.\n  - recipes: Joanna will bring some of her recipes to share desserts with Nate.\n  - feedback: Joanna received positive feedback that people are connecting with her writing, which Nate mentioned.\n  - cute notes: Joanna's brother wrote the cute notes, which reminds her of sweet memories from when they were kids.\n  - desserts: Joanna will bring some of her dessert recipes to share with Nate, building on a prior conversation where they discussed dairy-free dessert recipes.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - old notebooks: Joanna found old notebooks containing her early writings last week, showing her progress. Nate asked Joanna what she was working on in that notebook.\n  - characters: Joanna saw characters she wrote acted out on the big screen for the third time, finding the experience rewarding. Nate inquired about the character on the left in a shared photo.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - motivation: Joanna's cork board has inspiring quotes/pictures for motivation and creativity. She gains motivation from having someone to support her.\n  - early writings: Joanna's early writings, found in old notebooks last week, include elements of self-discovery that movie producers found interesting.\n  - journal: Joanna uses her journal as her rock while she is busy with writing projects, finding it helps her express feelings and heal.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - screenplay: Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that appeared on the big screen yesterday and submitted a recent screenplay to a film contest.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2053,"context_chars":8468,"retrieval_duration":0.3551309108734131,"response_duration":2.776301145553589,"total_duration":3.131432056427002,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer accurately reflects the topic of the gold answer by mentioning the blog post about a hard moment in Joanna's life.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question. It explicitly states that Joanna created an online blog post about a hard moment in her life, which is the exact content referenced in the golden answer. Additionally, it mentions that someone wrote her a letter in response to this blog post, confirming the connection between the content and the letter.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Joanna created an online blog post about a hard moment in her life","Someone wrote Joanna a letter in response to her online blog post"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_6","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_6_qa_28","category":"2","difficulty":"unknown","query":"When did James volunteer at an organization?","golden_answer":"May 2022","hypothesis":"James volunteered at an organization on June 19, 2022.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - James volunteered with non-profits last month, taking a picture during that time. (event_time: 2022-05-19T00:00:00Z)\n  - James volunteered with an organization that provides necessary items to those who are less fortunate (event_time: 2022-06-19T21:59:00Z)\n  - James helped those in need by volunteering with an organization (event_time: 2022-06-19T21:59:00Z)\n  - John asked James for more details about the organization James volunteered with. (event_time: 2022-06-19T21:59:00Z)\n  - The organization James volunteered with provides necessary items to those in need (event_time: 2022-06-19T21:59:00Z)\n  - James observed that little gifts can do a lot when volunteering. (event_time: 2022-05-19T00:00:00Z)\n  - James offered to help figure out some ideas for the project (event_time: 2022-04-23T11:04:00Z)\n  - James notes that combining gaming and volunteering is a great idea. (event_time: 2022-05-08T00:45:00Z)\n  - James asked John about how the volunteering affected him. (event_time: 2022-05-11T17:00:00Z)\n  - James asks John about the kind of volunteer gig that was offered. (event_time: 2022-10-03T09:20:00Z)\n  - James did something good on the way to visit Mark (event_time: 2022-11-07T20:57:00Z)\n  - A group of people brings their own ideas to James's endeavors. (event_time: 2022-05-04T19:01:00Z)\n  - James is associated with the passion shared by the group of people. (event_time: 2022-05-04T19:01:00Z)\n  - James did something good on the way to visit Josh (event_time: 2022-11-07T20:57:00Z)\n  - James believes helping animals is very important. (event_time: 2022-05-08T00:45:00Z)\n  - James participated in a hike last Thursday. (event_time: 2022-04-21T00:00:00Z)\n  - The volunteer gig is at a game dev non-profit (event_time: 2022-10-03T09:20:00Z)\n  - James has worked with Python. (event_time: 2022-03-17T15:47:00Z)\n  - James participated in bowling yesterday. (event_time: 2022-03-16T00:00:00Z)\n  - James met the whole team. (event_time: 2022-04-04T14:13:00Z)\n  - James is actively seeking ways to achieve self-improvement. (event_time: 2022-09-04T21:23:00Z)\n  - James started playing the game a few days ago (event_time: 2022-03-23T00:40:00Z)\n  - John asked James when James is returning. (event_time: 2022-07-09T17:13:00Z)\n  - James usually brings books when he is there. (event_time: 2022-06-16T17:07:00Z)\n  - The project James is excited about involves the main character. (event_time: 2022-03-17T15:47:00Z)\n  - James seems to strongly support the team. (event_time: 2022-06-13T16:30:00Z)\n  - James asked that 'us' share impressions when trying something (event_time: 2022-05-04T19:01:00Z)\n  - James made his first game recently. (event_time: 2022-10-13T14:14:00Z)\n  - James did not make it to the end of the online gaming tournament. (event_time: 2022-04-04T14:13:00Z)\n  - James built a website. (event_time: 2022-03-17T15:47:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - the organization: John developed software for a charitable foundation to streamline operations, replacing manual paper record-keeping and inventory management with a smartphone application. John asked for details about the organization James volunteered with.\n  - James: James is conversing with John about John's new volunteer role as a programming mentor for game developers.\n  - John: John expressed interest in seeing the impact of gifts and asked James for more information about the organization James volunteered with.\n  - James: James is on a road trip, visited friends Josh and Mark, and visited an animal sanctuary with rescue dogs. He is collaborating with John.\n  - gifts: John asked James about the impact of gifts and requested more details about the organization James volunteered with.\n  - James: James expressed enthusiasm for John's programming work for a charitable foundation and requested visual examples of the software's impact.\n  - James: James reacted positively to John's gaming tournament for charity, noting gaming brings people together. James also mentioned renting an apartment near McGee's bar.\n  - James: James discussed John's new online programming group and mentioned his dog joined him while he was playing on the console.\n  - James: James expressed that John's use of programming skills for a charitable foundation's software tool was awesome and important, and he would like to see visual examples of the impact.\n  - James: James is on a road trip, visited friends Josh and Mark, and has dogs that make dark days better. James is an assistant.\n  - James: James created a game, inspired by Witcher 3, and was fulfilled seeing players engage. He recently adopted a pup named Ned from a Stamford shelter and organized an online programming competition with John.\n  - James: James is currently on a road trip, visited friends Josh and Mark, and inquired about John's online board game project.\n  - James: James, an assistant, asked John about his activities and encouraged him about freelancing for gaining experience and problem-solving.\n  - James: James is an assistant who greeted John and asked about his fun activities and current projects.\n  - James: James went on a road trip with family and dogs yesterday. He congratulated John on winning the regional chess tournament and offered to play chess after John practices.\n  - James: Three days ago, James lost power in his apartment while playing a game, resulting in lost progress due to forgetting to save. James has a dog named Ned and knows John's siblings signed up for programming.\n  - James: James started a road trip with family and dogs yesterday. He congratulated John on winning the regional chess tournament and offered chess opening resources.\n  - James: Three days ago, James lost power in his apartment, interrupting a game. Two days ago, his mother visited with her army friend.\n  - James: James conversed with John, asking about his activities and acknowledging freelancing as a good skill-sharpening method.\n  - James: James recently made and released his first game for the gaming community, finding it fulfilling to see players engage with his creation.\n  - James: James congratulated John on getting a dream job. James is lucky to have two people who always help him when he is struggling.\n  - James: James is on a road trip, visited friends Josh and Mark, complimented the name Luna, and later said goodbye to John.\n  - James: James is working on a project that hit a major snag due to a bug in the code messing up game mechanics; he was unable to solve it after hours of debugging. He previously adopted a pup named Ned last week in Stamford.\n  - James: James asked Samantha to be his girlfriend at the theater, and she agreed. They visited McGee's bar, where Samantha enjoyed a lager. James thanked John for support and hopes to cook for him soon.\n