rk: Joanna finished a cute little bookmark for a lady at her writing club. Nate commented that the bookmark is great and she will love it.\n  - favorite game: Joanna asked Nate what his favorite game is after he won a Valorant tournament.\n  - gaming videos: Joanna asked Nate what inspired him to start making gaming videos.\n  - things to watch: Nate told Joanna he will give her a shout whenever he runs out of things to watch.\n  - the trail: Joanna found an awesome, gorgeous hiking trail in her hometown. Nate is curious to see what the trail looks like and heard there is a nice trail just north of where he lives.\n  - similar interests: Joanna and Nate established they have similar interests, leading Joanna to ask Nate about his preferred movie types.\n  - fantasy movies: Nate likes fantasy movies because they spark his imagination, following Joanna's question about his favorite fantasy or sci-fi movie.\n  - Nate: Nate congratulated Joanna on filming her movie from her road-trip script, asked about the coolest on-set moment, and commented that her food looked yummy with nice colors and kick.\n  - advice: Joanna gave advice to Nate after his game tournament was pushed back and he didn't make the finals. Nate acknowledged the advice.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - that movie: Joanna watched 'that movie' about 3 years ago and acquired a physical copy.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - Nate: Nate praised Joanna for setting up meetings with movie producers, comparing her success to winning a video game tournament, and expressed pride in her feeling hopeful and inspired.\n  - wat