ing people, which he views as a career start.\n  - John's siblings: John's siblings signed up for programming and are playing a simple, text-based adventure game to work on coding skills.\n  - John: John confirmed his dog's name is Ned. His siblings signed up for programming and are playing a text-based adventure game.\n  - John: John is working on his first professional website project for a local small business, outside of classwork.\n  - John: John won the regional chess tournament. He also had a fun weekend working with a game developer on a project where his ideas were implemented.\n  - game designs: John's siblings are coding while playing a simple, text-based adventure game. James asked John about new game designs.\n  - John: John is excited to start volunteering as a programming mentor for a game dev non-profit, teaching coding and assisting with projects. He is meeting with James.\n  - game: Three days ago, James lost power during a game (Mario). John collaborated with a developer on an online board game and was asked if it has been released.\n  - text-based adventure game: John's siblings signed up for programming and are learning coding using a text-based adventure game.\n  - game development: John congratulated James on releasing his game and praised his determination and love for game development, anticipating future creations.\n  - John: John collaborated with a game developer on an online board game and appreciates dogs for the joy and positivity they bring.\n  - John: John volunteered for a charitable foundation creating software. He recently placed second in a local tournament last Friday, noting the competitive energy was insane.\n  - mobile applications: John asked James if he likes the idea of developing mobile applications together in the future.\n  - John: John is working on his first professional website project for a local small business and asked James about Civilization VI.\n  - John: John shared that he got his dream job after many intervi